  "body": "## What changed\n\n3D Pocket now refuses an upright job before building its path when a wider shank or holder reaches the material at Bottom Z.\nThe message names the tool and band.\nIt tells the user to raise Bottom of Part Z or use a longer-reaching tool.\nThe check reads the same neck and holder bands as verification.\nExact contact also refuses.\n\nThis is a conservative depth check.\nIt does not credit lateral room, previously removed stock, or stock to leave.\nA deep cut with enough lateral room can therefore refuse.\nThe existing tilted whole-model refusal keeps precedence.\n\nThe existing run_job wrapper moves into a small child module.\nIts public API and generation arms stay unchanged.\nThe decision is recorded in docs/decisions/1844-pocket3d-reach.md.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe level ladder proves only flute-radius clearance.\nA wider shank or holder can touch a tall wall while generation reports ok.\nVerification correctly blocks posting afterward.\nThis fix leaves those verification laws unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins failed before the fix and passed afterward:\n\n- the_sample_as_imported_roughs_the_3d_pocket_beside_its_silhouette\n- a_closed_cavity_refuses_the_wider_shank_by_name\n- a_closed_cavity_refuses_the_holder_with_a_flute_width_shank\n- a_wider_shank_touching_the_wall_top_is_refused\n\nControls pass for a shallower bottom, longer flutes, a flute-width shank, and a 0.001 mm axial gap.\nAll six pocket3d_reach tests and all five shared_face_bodies tests pass.\n\nMutation checks each failed red and passed green after restoration:\n\n- Restore generate.rs from upstream/main to bypass the preflight.\n- Disable the shank check.\n- Disable the holder check.\n- Replace the contact comparison >= with >.\n\ncargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main passed in 362 seconds.\ncargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\ngit diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine run or interactive UI run.\nNo new tilted-pocket planner or per-level assembly avoidance.\nThe new pins use catalog cylindrical tools.\nThey do not separately exercise a modeled holder or neck through this preflight.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPRs #1817, #1782, and #1713 touch generate.rs in run_job_arms.\nThis change moves and edits run_job.\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThe branch starts at upstream/main 62e1d36a655a71407ff7a9980057db3c8cc8197a.\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket refuses depths with unproved shank or holder clearance before generation and names the tool and Bottom Z remedy.\n\nFixes #1844\n",
